Prettier formats the code and does not lint. `.prettierrc` sets the style (semicolons, single quotes, trailing commas, 100 columns) and sorts Tailwind classes, including the ones inside `cn` and `clsx` calls.

`.prettierignore` keeps these out of it:

- build output and lockfiles
{{#if (has "stack" "tanstack-start")}}
- the generated route tree
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "orm" "drizzle")}}
- the Drizzle migrations
{{/if}}

`{{runScript "format"}}` rewrites the files and `{{runScript "format:check"}}` only reports the files that differ.{{#if (has "linter" "eslint-prettier")}} ESLint does the linting, with `eslint-config-prettier` turning off the ESLint rules that conflict with the formatter.{{/if}}
